  "notes": [
    "Payment races: store who holds the seat and until when (held_by, held_until). Confirm with a conditional update (sold WHERE held_by = this fan AND held_until > now). If the hold was lost while the payment was processing, refund. Many sites also extend the hold while a payment is in progress.",
    "Another option: authorize first and capture after the seat is confirmed; it avoids the refund, at the cost of more states to manage and an authorization that can expire.",
    "Idempotency keys are documented by Stripe, Adyen and PayPal. The price: the provider remembers each key for a limited time, so a retry has to arrive inside that window. Store the key with the order before calling the provider.",
    "Payments are asynchronous too: webhooks can arrive late or twice, so deduplicate by event id, and run a reconciliation job to catch charged-but-not-sold seats."
  ],
